==English==

===Etymology===
Modification of English [[-orama]], influenced by [[diorama]] and [[panorama]], and thus from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|ὅραμα|ὅρᾱμᾰ|sight”, “spectacle}} and ultimately {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*wer-}}, meaning to perceive or look out for.

===Suffix===
{{head|en|suffixes}}

# Alteration of [[-orama]], used in suffixing a word ending with an ''r'' or vowel sound, for example,
#: ''camera'' to form ''camerarama'' or
#: ''future'' to form (eliding the ''e'' and merging the two ''r''s into one) ''futurama''

====Usage notes====
* The suffix is usually appended without hyphenation, or occasionally with hyphen intended to catch the eye.

